# The HUD menu's Video drop-down: Set GStreamer Source and GStreamer Stop, played through this
# machine's GStreamer runtime into the HUD's background.
#
# The claim: Set GStreamer Source asks "GStreamer url", "Enter the source pipeline ...", starting
# at the C#'s test pipeline when gstreamer_url is not saved (FlightData.cs:4927-4935). OK saves
# the pipeline as gstreamer_url, finds the runtime (LookForGstreamer, GStreamer.cs:1417-1485) and
# plays it (hudGStreamer.Start, GStreamer.cs:1183-1349): here gst-launch-1.0 runs the pipeline
# with its `appsink name=outsink` turned into PNG frames on its output, and each frame is the
# HUD's picture as MainV2's OnNewImage makes it (MainV2.cs:3428-3447). `videotestsrc` with no
# caps settles on 320 x 240. GStreamer Stop ends it and the picture goes (GStreamer.cs:1491-1495,
# 1341-1343). Asked again, the box holds the saved pipeline; Cancel stops (FlightData.cs:4960-4963).
#
# Needs the GStreamer runtime (gst-launch-1.0 on the PATH, with the base and good plugins); no
# vehicle. The unit tests in crates/mp-video/src/gstreamer.rs run the same pipeline headless.
# Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-gstreamer.gui

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 12
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

expect fly.hud.gstreamer false
expect fly.hud.gstreamer.pipeline none
expect hud.camera none

# The question, at the C#'s first pipeline.
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
expect fly.hud.menu true
click fly-hud-video
expect fly.hud.menu.video true
click fly-hud-gstreamer
expect fly.hud.menu false
# `fly.prompt` is the box's question, as the other scripts read it; "GStreamer url" is its title.
expect fly.prompt ~ Enter the source pipeline
expect fly.prompt.value ~ videotestsrc ! video/x-raw, width=1280, height=720
key ctrl+u
type videotestsrc pattern=red ! appsink name=outsink
expect fly.prompt.value videotestsrc pattern=red ! appsink name=outsink

# OK: the pipeline plays, its frames the HUD's picture.
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.hud.gstreamer true
expect fly.hud.gstreamer.pipeline videotestsrc pattern=red ! appsink name=outsink
expect fly.hud.gstreamer.frames > 10
expect fly.hud.gstreamer.frame 320x240
expect fly.hud.gstreamer.error none
expect hud.camera 320x240

# GStreamer Stop: the launcher ended, the picture gone.
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-video
click fly-hud-gstreamerstop
expect fly.hud.menu false
expect fly.hud.gstreamer false
expect hud.camera none

# Asked again, the saved pipeline in the box; Cancel stops and plays nothing.
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-video
click fly-hud-gstreamer
# `fly.prompt` is the box's question, as the other scripts read it; "GStreamer url" is its title.
expect fly.prompt ~ Enter the source pipeline
expect fly.prompt.value videotestsrc pattern=red ! appsink name=outsink
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.hud.gstreamer false
expect hud.camera none
